# Round 58: pins the observe carve-out in the top-level order guard.
# `observe of v` on an UNBOUND name is VM-tolerated (rc 0, silent no-op --
# while `print of v` in the same position dies rc 1; filed upstream as a
# silent-tolerance divergence), so a bare-ident observe argument is not a
# use for the order guard. The guard's first version refused this VM-valid
# program, evicting an observer form that was previously in the envelope.
observe of v
v is 2
print of v
